 "notes": "FASER search for a->gamma gamma with 57.7 fb^-1 at sqrt(s)=13.6 TeV; 1 event observed vs 0.44+-0.39 expected. The paper's primary model is the ALP-W coupling g_aWW (Fig. 10), which has no canonical plane here; reported instead is the paper's own ALP-photon interpretation (observed 90% CL limit, blue curve in Fig. 11 left / Fig. 17b), which is natively in the g_agamma vs m_a plane. The excluded region is a closed band: points trace the lower boundary from the plot's left edge (m_a~10 MeV, g~5.8e-4 GeV^-1) with increasing mass to the tip at ~72 MeV (g~1.2e-4 GeV^-1), then the upper boundary back with decreasing mass to the top of the frame (~14.7 MeV, g~1e-2 GeV^-1); mass is therefore not monotonic over the full list. Extracted programmatically by colour from the e-print raster figure figs/alpphoton_final_col.png with log-axis tick calibration (~1% accuracy). Collider/beam-dump-type limit: no dark-matter density assumption.",
